  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "BREAKING: targets net10.0 only (runs on .NET 10 and later, tested on .NET 10 and .NET 11); Error is now a sealed class (error.Type, not error.Value.Type); SuccessKind.None is the default and failures carry it; default(Result<T>) and default(Result) now throw from IsSuccess, Map, Match and every To*Result instead of reporting success; Result.AcceptedLocation is renamed Location; Error.BadRequest takes IReadOnlyDictionary; a Result, Result<T> or Error returned from an endpoint without mapping now throws instead of going out as 200; EF Core 40001/40P01 (serialization failure, deadlock) now reach the 500 handler instead of 409; ToProblemResult() and the void Result controller methods return ActionResult; ResultCrafterLogger and ProblemDetailsEnricher are internal; ResultCrafter.MediatR is discontinued. Fixed: error responses keep the house shape whatever the order of AddControllers() and AddResultCrafter() and whatever the Accept header; WithValidation skips validation after a parameter binding failure; AddResultCrafterValidation registers internal validators; the 500 handler honors ExceptionHandlerOptions.StatusCodeSelector; .NET 11 unreadable JSON bodies and built-in AddValidation() responses get the house BadRequest shape with JSON field keys. Added: typed Error.With() overloads for extra ProblemDetails members (NativeAOT-safe), Error.TooManyRequests(retryAfter) with the Retry-After header, the ProblemResponse OpenAPI schema on all Produces* helpers, and a NativeAOT smoke test in CI. Upgrading from 2.x: https://github.com/HaikAsatryan/ResultCrafter/blob/main/docs/migrating-to-3.md",
